# Two checks that shellcheck leaves optional. SC2312 fired on this repo's own
# draft-release workflow; SC2249 recurred across review rounds on the publish
# workflow. Neither is on by default:
#
#   SC2249  a `case` with no default arm — an unmatched value falls through
#           silently, which in a publish guard means a member classified as
#           neither published nor absent.
#   SC2312  a return value masked by a command substitution or process
#           substitution — `set -e` does not see through either, so a script
#           that refuses is read by its caller as one that succeeded.
#
# actionlint runs shellcheck with `--norc`, so this file does not apply to
# workflow `run:` blocks. The actionlint hook in prek.toml carries the same
# options as its own `env` instead; keep the two lists in step. This file
# governs standalone shell scripts, in CI and locally alike.
enable=add-default-case,check-extra-masked-returns
